  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Harnessing the potential of AI for Human Rights in the GCC countries</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This workplan will be focusing on building the capacities of the judiciary in the GCC region on AI and Human rights. Several judicial systems in the region have already started their digitalization, including AI to their work. While in KSA the Judiciary is already fully embracing digitalization and proceeding with trials and ruling online, in Qatar since May 2023, Public prosecution is using AI tools to facilitate and optimize its work, and the Ministry of Justice announced in September 2023, its willingness to fully use the potential of AI to enhance Qatar&apos;s legal system. Building on that momentum, the funds will be used as seed funding to organize a regional training on AI and the Rule of Law for the Judiciary.

The RP budget will be used as seed funding to organize the pilot regional training that will be targeting around 40 judges from 10 countries in the region (including all the countries of the GCC) and advocate for the funding of the project document &quot;AI and the Rule of Law in the Arab region&quot;.</narrative>
  </description>
